# {{NAME}}

An [Open Conduit](https://github.com/open-conduit/open-conduit) extension package in TypeScript. It serves one toolbelt operation, `{{NAME}}.hello`, that agents call through Open Conduit.

Run `npm install`, then `make check`.

## What to change first

1. **The operation.** In `src/extension.ts`, rename `{{NAME}}.hello`, change its `input` schema and what its handler returns, and say in `guidance` when an agent should call it. Add operations, sources (`ingressType`), routes, Work kinds, tasks and checks the same way: each registration on `build()` also declares it in the manifest.
2. **The tests.** `src/extension.test.ts` calls the operation on the SDK's in-memory test host (`@open-conduit/sdk/testing`). Change it to match.
3. **The certification fixture.** `certification(...)` in `src/extension.ts` holds the cases `make certify` checks; give each operation a case.
4. **The playbook.** `playbooks/{{NAME}}.md` tells agents what the package does for them.

The guide to the SDK, the test host and certification is [Writing an extension in TypeScript](https://open-conduit.github.io/open-conduit/architecture/extension-packaging/#writing-an-extension-in-typescript).

## Commands

- `make check`: what CI runs, the formatting, the typecheck, the tests and `make package`.
- `make package`: the package directory in `dist/{{NAME}}`, as Open Conduit installs it.
- `make lint`: `open-conduit extension check` on the package.
- `make certify`: certifies the package with the `open-conduit` on PATH (or `OPEN_CONDUIT=...`).

CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) runs `make check`, and lints and certifies the package against Open Conduit's `main` and its latest release.

`make package` bundles the extension as CommonJS, gives the package its own `package.json` saying so, and starts the executable with the absolute path of the Node that packaged it. The daemon then runs it with that Node, whatever its own PATH finds. After changing Node (with a version manager, say), run `make package` again before installing.

Install the built package with `open-conduit extension install dist/{{NAME}}`; it takes effect at the next `open-conduit serve`.
